IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa-definitions`
IMPORT `coa12-logic`

-- coa12-ch4b-resignation.l4: the Companies Act 2006, Part 16, Chapter 4, from "Resignation of auditor" to the end of the Chapter:
-- ss 516, 517, 518, 519, 519A, 520, 521, 522, 523, 524, 525, 526 (lines 7250-7415 of ukpga-2006-46.txt).
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively. See coa12-ch3a-report.l4 for how to read an answer. Forks are in NOTES.md.
-- s 517 is blank in this text (repealed). Subsections (2) to (4) of s 522 do not appear in this text at all (NOTES.md, finding).
-- Keel and other-part answers are INPUTS named as PLAN.md 4.1 and 4.2 name them.
-- Periods are counted day by day: "within 14 days after" is both ends in (coa12 helper); "the period of 14 days beginning with the day"
-- is the day and the 13 after it; "not less than 14 days before" is on or before the day 14 earlier (fork F9).

-- =========================================================================================================
-- s 516  Resignation of auditor
-- =========================================================================================================

-- COVERS: s 516(1)
-- Plain gloss: an auditor may resign by sending the company a notice.
-- src:7252 | (1) An auditor of a company may resign his office by sending a notice to that effect to the company.
@ref s 516(1) Resignation by notice (src:7252-7252)
GIVEN `the person is an auditor of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the auditor has sent a notice to that effect to the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 516(1) the auditor may resign his office by sending a notice` MEANS
    IF `the person is an auditor of the company` AND `the auditor has sent a notice to that effect to the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An auditor of a company may resign his office by sending a notice to that effect to the company"

-- COVERS: s 516(2)
-- Plain gloss: where the company is a public interest company the notice is not effective unless it comes with the s 519 statement. The answer is the BAR: JUST TRUE means the notice is not effective.
-- src:7253 | (2) Where the company is a public interest company, the notice is not effective unless it is accompanied by the statement required by section 519.
@ref s 516(2) A public interest company: the statement must accompany the notice (src:7253-7253)
GIVEN `s 519A(1) the company is a public interest company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the notice is accompanied by the statement required by section 519` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 516(2) the notice of resignation is not effective` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 519A(1) the company is a public interest company`
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the company is a public interest company, the notice is not effective unless ..." (the bar is for a public interest company only: the 2026-11-05 ruling on "where")
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the company is a public interest company borrows terms of other instruments (s 519A)
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF `the notice is accompanied by the statement required by section 519`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the notice is not effective unless it is accompanied by the statement required by section 519" (an "unless" met: fork F6)
        ELSE JUST TRUE

-- COVERS: s 516(3)
-- Plain gloss: an effective notice ends the auditor's term on the day it is received, or on a later date it names.
-- src:7254 | (3) An effective notice of resignation operates to bring the auditor's term of office to an end as of the date on which the notice is received or on such later date as may be specified in it.
@ref s 516(3) When the term of office ends (src:7254-7254)
GIVEN `the notice of resignation is effective` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date on which the notice is received` IS A DATE
      `a later date specified in the notice` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 516(3) the day on which the auditor's term of office ends` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the notice of resignation is effective`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An effective notice of resignation operates to bring the auditor's term of office to an end"
    ELSE CONSIDER `a later date specified in the notice`
         WHEN JUST d THEN IF d GREATER THAN `the date on which the notice is received` THEN JUST d ELSE JUST `the date on which the notice is received`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST `the date on which the notice is received`

-- =========================================================================================================
-- s 518  Rights of resigning auditor
-- =========================================================================================================

-- COVERS: s 518(1), s 518(1)(a), s 518(1)(b)
-- Plain gloss: s 518 applies where the resignation notice comes with an s 519 statement, except where the company is not a public interest company and the statement says A considers there is nothing members or creditors need to be told.
-- src:7258 | (1) This section applies where an auditor's (A's) notice of resignation is accompanied by a statement under section 519 except where—.
-- src:7259 | (a) the company is a non-public interest company, and
-- src:7260 | (b) the statement includes a statement to the effect that A considers that none of the reasons for A's ceasing to hold office, and no matters (if any) connected with A's ceasing to hold office, need to be brought to the attention of members or creditors of the company (as required by section 519(3B)).
@ref s 518(1) Where the section applies (src:7258-7260)
GIVEN `the auditor's notice of resignation is accompanied by a statement under section 519` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 519A(1) the company is a non-public interest company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the statement includes a statement to the effect that A considers that none of the reasons for A's ceasing to hold office, and no matters (if any) connected with A's ceasing to hold office, need to be brought to the attention of members or creditors of the company (as required by section 519(3B))` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 518(1) the section applies to the resigning auditor` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the auditor's notice of resignation is accompanied by a statement under section 519`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies where an auditor's (A's) notice of resignation is accompanied by a statement under section 519" (the 2026-11-05 ruling on "where")
    ELSE CONSIDER `coa12 both answers hold` `s 519A(1) the company is a non-public interest company` (`coa12 the answer for the fact` `the statement includes a statement to the effect that A considers that none of the reasons for A's ceasing to hold office, and no matters (if any) connected with A's ceasing to hold office, need to be brought to the attention of members or creditors of the company (as required by section 519(3B))`)
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except where— (a) the company is a non-public interest company, and (b) the statement includes a statement to the effect that A considers that none of the reasons ... need to be brought to the attention of members or creditors" (an "except" met: fork F6)
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): whether the company is a non-public interest company rests on s 519A, which defines only "public interest company" (fork F10)

-- COVERS: s 518(2)
-- Plain gloss: A may send with the notice an authenticated requisition calling on the directors to convene a general meeting at once, to hear his explanation of the reasons for, and matters connected with, his resignation.
-- src:7261 | (2) He may send with the notice an authenticated requisition calling on the directors of the company forthwith duly to convene a general meeting of the company for the purpose of receiving and considering such explanation of the reasons for, and matters connected with, his resignation as he may wish to place before the meeting.
@ref s 518(2) The requisition for a general meeting (src:7261-7261)
GIVEN `s 518(1) the section applies to the resigning auditor` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 1146 Requirement of authentication` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the requisition is sent with the notice of resignation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requisition calls on the directors to convene a general meeting forthwith for the purpose of receiving and considering such explanation of the reasons for, and matters connected with, his resignation as he may wish to place before the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 518(2) the auditor may send with the notice an authenticated requisition calling on the directors to convene a general meeting` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 518(1) the section applies to the resigning auditor`
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies where ... except where" (subsection (1) not met)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the section applies is subsection (1) and rests on s 519A
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF `s 1146 Requirement of authentication` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `the requisition is sent with the notice of resignation` AND `the requisition calls on the directors to convene a general meeting forthwith for the purpose of receiving and considering such explanation of the reasons for, and matters connected with, his resignation as he may wish to place before the meeting`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "He may send with the notice an authenticated requisition calling on the directors of the company forthwith duly to convene a general meeting of the company for the purpose of receiving and considering such explanation"

-- COVERS: s 518(3), s 518(3)(a), s 518(3)(b), s 518(3)#L7265
-- Plain gloss: A may ask the company to circulate to members a written statement (not unreasonably long) of the reasons for, and matters connected with, his resignation, before the meeting he has requisitioned or before a general meeting where his term would have ended or his place is to be filled.
-- src:7262 | (3) He may request the company to circulate to its members—
-- src:7263 | (a) before the meeting convened on his requisition, or
-- src:7264 | (b) before any general meeting at which his term of office would otherwise have expired or at which it is proposed to fill the vacancy caused by his resignation,
-- src:7265 | a statement in writing (not exceeding a reasonable length) of the reasons for, and matters connected with, his resignation.
@ref s 518(3) The request to circulate a statement (src:7262-7265)
GIVEN `s 518(1) the section applies to the resigning auditor` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the statement is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement does not exceed a reasonable length` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the circulation is requested before the meeting convened on his requisition, or before a general meeting at which his term of office would otherwise have expired or at which it is proposed to fill the vacancy caused by his resignation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 518(3) the auditor may request the company to circulate a statement of reasons to its members` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 518(1) the section applies to the resigning auditor`
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies where ... except where" (subsection (1) not met)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the section applies is subsection (1) and rests on s 519A
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF `the statement is in writing` AND `the statement does not exceed a reasonable length` AND `the circulation is requested before the meeting convened on his requisition, or before a general meeting at which his term of office would otherwise have expired or at which it is proposed to fill the vacancy caused by his resignation`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "He may request the company to circulate to its members— (a) before the meeting convened on his requisition, or (b) before any general meeting ..., a statement in writing (not exceeding a reasonable length)"

-- COVERS: s 518(4), s 518(4)(a), s 518(4)(b)
-- Plain gloss: unless the statement arrives too late, the company must say in its notice of the meeting that it was made and send a copy to every member sent the notice.
-- src:7266 | (4) The company must (unless the statement is received too late for it to comply)—
-- src:7267 | (a) in any notice of the meeting given to members of the company, state the fact of the statement having been made, and
-- src:7268 | (b) send a copy of the statement to every member of the company to whom notice of the meeting is or has been sent.
@ref s 518(4) What the company must do with the statement (src:7266-7268)
GIVEN `s 518(1) the section applies to the resigning auditor` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the auditor has made a request under subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement is received too late for the company to comply` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 518(4) the company must state the fact of the statement in its notice of the meeting and send a copy to every member to whom the notice is sent` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 518(1) the section applies to the resigning auditor`
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies where ... except where" (subsection (1) not met)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the section applies is subsection (1) and rests on s 519A
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF (NOT `the auditor has made a request under subsection (3)`)
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection presupposes a request and says nothing where there is none
        ELSE IF `the statement is received too late for the company to comply`
             THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The company must (unless the statement is received too late for it to comply)" (fork F6: an "unless" once met)
             ELSE JUST TRUE

-- COVERS-FORK F11: s 518(5)
-- Plain gloss: on a requisition, the directors must within 21 days of the company receiving it proceed duly to convene a meeting, for a day not more than 28 days after the notice convening it is given.
-- src:7269 | (5) The directors must within 21 days from the date on which the company receives a requisition under this section proceed duly to convene a meeting for a day not more than 28 days after the date on which the notice convening the meeting is given.
@ref s 518(5) The directors must convene the meeting (src:7269-7269)
GIVEN `s 518(1) the section applies to the resigning auditor` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the company has received a requisition under this section` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 518(5) the directors must convene the meeting` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 518(1) the section applies to the resigning auditor`
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies where ... except where" (subsection (1) not met)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the section applies is subsection (1) and rests on s 519A
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF `the company has received a requisition under this section`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The directors must within 21 days from the date on which the company receives a requisition under this section proceed duly to convene a meeting" (fork F1: a duty whose trigger is unmet)

@ref s 518(5) The directors must convene the meeting within the periods (src:7269-7269)
GIVEN `the date on which the company receives the requisition` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the notice convening the meeting is given` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day for which the meeting is convened` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 518(5) the directors convened the meeting within the periods the subsection allows` MEANS
    IF (NOT (`coa12 the act was done within the number of days after the day` `the date on which the notice convening the meeting is given` `the date on which the company receives the requisition` 21))
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within 21 days from the date on which the company receives a requisition" (a period fixed in the text's own words: the 2026-11-05 ruling (a); "proceed duly to convene" read as giving the notice convening the meeting: fork F11)
    ELSE CONSIDER `the date on which the notice convening the meeting is given`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within 21 days" (no notice convening the meeting was given)
         WHEN JUST notice THEN
             IF `the day for which the meeting is convened` GREATER THAN notice PLUS 28
             THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "for a day not more than 28 days after the date on which the notice convening the meeting is given"
             ELSE JUST TRUE

-- The 21 days as a deontic rule: the duty to convene runs from the day the company receives the requisition (day 0). The 28-day limit on the
-- date of the meeting is a limit on what is convened, not a second duty of the directors, and is left to the decision function above.
@ref s 518(5) The directors must convene the meeting (src:7269-7269)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Action of a party`
`s 518(5) the directors' duty to convene the meeting` MEANS
    PARTY Director
    MUST `Action of a party` OF Director, Auditor, "proceed duly to convene a meeting"
    WITHIN 21
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Director BECAUSE "s 518(5): the directors did not proceed duly to convene a meeting within 21 days from the date on which the company received the requisition"

-- COVERS: s 518(6)
-- Plain gloss: if the directors default under (5), every director who failed to take all reasonable steps to secure that a meeting was convened commits an offence.
-- src:7270 | (6) If default is made in complying with subsection (5), every director who failed to take all reasonable steps to secure that a meeting was convened commits an offence.
@ref s 518(6) The offence (src:7270-7270)
GIVEN `default is made in complying with subsection (5)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director failed to take all reasonable steps to secure that a meeting was convened` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 518(6) the director commits an offence` MEANS
    IF `default is made in complying with subsection (5)` AND `the director failed to take all reasonable steps to secure that a meeting was convened`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If default is made in complying with subsection (5), every director who failed to take all reasonable steps to secure that a meeting was convened commits an offence" (marginal reading (a))

-- COVERS: s 518(7), s 518(7)(a), s 518(7)(b)
-- Plain gloss: the penalty: on indictment a fine; on summary conviction a fine up to the statutory maximum.
-- src:7271 | (7) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable—
-- src:7272 | (a) on conviction on indictment, to a fine;
-- src:7273 | (b) on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum.
@ref s 518(7) The penalty (src:7271-7273)
GIVEN mode IS A `Mode of conviction`
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 518(7) the penalty for an offence under this section` MEANS
    CONSIDER mode
    WHEN `on conviction on indictment` THEN JUST (Penalty OF mode, NOTHING, JUST `a fine without a stated limit`, NOTHING, FALSE)
    OTHERWISE JUST (Penalty OF mode, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` OF 1), NOTHING, FALSE)

-- COVERS: s 518(8)
-- Plain gloss: if a copy of the statement is not sent out because it arrived too late or because of the company's default, the auditor may require it to be read out at the meeting.
-- src:7274 | (8) If a copy of the statement mentioned above is not sent out as required because received too late or because of the company's default, the auditor may (without prejudice to his right to be heard orally) require that the statement be read out at the meeting.
@ref s 518(8) The auditor may require the statement to be read out (src:7274-7274)
GIVEN `s 518(1) the section applies to the resigning auditor` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `a copy of the statement is not sent out as required` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that is because the statement was received too late` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that is because of the company's default` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 518(8) the auditor may require that the statement be read out at the meeting` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 518(1) the section applies to the resigning auditor`
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies where ... except where" (subsection (1) not met)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the section applies is subsection (1) and rests on s 519A
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF `a copy of the statement is not sent out as required` AND (`that is because the statement was received too late` OR `that is because of the company's default`)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If a copy of the statement mentioned above is not sent out as required because received too late or because of the company's default, the auditor may ... require that the statement be read out at the meeting" (fork F16: a grant named "may" whose plain "if" gate fails; the other reading is JUST FALSE)

-- COVERS: s 518(9), s 518(9)#L7276
-- Plain gloss: copies need not be sent or the statement read out if, on application, the court is satisfied the auditor is using the section for needless publicity for defamatory matter; the court may order the auditor to pay costs.
-- src:7275 | (9) Copies of a statement need not be sent out and the statement need not be read out at the meeting if, on the application either of the company or of any other person who claims to be aggrieved, the court is satisfied that the auditor is using the provisions of this section to secure needless publicity for defamatory matter.
-- src:7276 | The court may order the company's costs (in Scotland, expenses) on such an application to be paid in whole or in part by the auditor, notwithstanding that he is not a party to the application.
@ref s 518(9) Needless publicity for defamatory matter (src:7275-7276)
GIVEN `an application has been made either by the company or by any other person who claims to be aggrieved` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied that the auditor is using the provisions of this section to secure needless publicity for defamatory matter` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 518(9) copies of the statement need not be sent out and the statement need not be read out at the meeting` MEANS
    IF `an application has been made either by the company or by any other person who claims to be aggrieved` AND `the court is satisfied that the auditor is using the provisions of this section to secure needless publicity for defamatory matter`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Copies of a statement need not be sent out and the statement need not be read out at the meeting if, on the application either of the company or of any other person who claims to be aggrieved, the court is satisfied that the auditor is using the provisions of this section to secure needless publicity for defamatory matter"

@ref s 518(9) closing words: costs (src:7276-7276)
GIVEN `the application has been made under subsection (9)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 518(9) the court may order the company's costs on the application to be paid in whole or in part by the auditor` MEANS
    IF `the application has been made under subsection (9)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The court may order the company's costs ... on such an application"

-- COVERS: s 518(10)
-- Plain gloss: an auditor who has resigned keeps his s 502(2) rights for any meeting mentioned in (3)(a) or (b).
-- src:7277 | (10) An auditor who has resigned has, notwithstanding his resignation, the rights conferred by section 502(2) in relation to any such general meeting of the company as is mentioned in subsection (3)(a) or (b) above.
@ref s 518(10) The resigned auditor's rights (src:7277-7277)
GIVEN `s 518(1) the section applies to the resigning auditor` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the auditor has resigned` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the meeting is one mentioned in subsection (3)(a) or (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 518(10) the resigned auditor has the rights conferred by section 502(2) in relation to the meeting` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 518(1) the section applies to the resigning auditor`
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies where ... except where" (subsection (1) not met)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the section applies is subsection (1) and rests on s 519A
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF `the auditor has resigned` AND `the meeting is one mentioned in subsection (3)(a) or (b)`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An auditor who has resigned has, notwithstanding his resignation, the rights conferred by section 502(2) in relation to any such general meeting of the company as is mentioned in subsection (3)(a) or (b)"

-- COVERS: s 518(10)#L7278
-- Plain gloss: in that case "matters concerning the auditor as auditor" in s 502(2) are read as matters concerning him as a former auditor.
-- src:7278 | In such a case the references in that section to matters concerning the auditor as auditor shall be construed as references to matters concerning him as a former auditor.
@ref s 518(10) closing words: matters concerning him as a former auditor (src:7278-7278)
GIVEN `s 518(10) the resigned auditor has the rights conferred by section 502(2) in relation to the meeting` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the auditor attends the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the part of the business of the meeting concerns him as a former auditor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 518(10) the resigned auditor is entitled to be heard on the part of the business` MEANS
    IF `s 518(10) the resigned auditor has the rights conferred by section 502(2) in relation to the meeting` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `the auditor attends the meeting` AND `the part of the business of the meeting concerns him as a former auditor`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In such a case the references in that section to matters concerning the auditor as auditor shall be construed as references to matters concerning him as a former auditor"

-- =========================================================================================================
-- s 519A  Meaning of "public interest company", "non-public interest company" and "exempt reasons"
-- (placed before s 519 in this file because s 519 and the sections after it use its answers)
-- =========================================================================================================

-- COVERS: s 519A(2)"issuer"
-- Plain gloss: "issuer" means what Part 6 of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 says (s 102A(6)): a borrowed answer, taken as an input.
-- src:7316 | (2) For the purposes of the definition of “public interest company”—
-- src:7317 | “issuer” has the same meaning as in Part 6 of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 (see section 102A(6));
@ref s 519A(2) "issuer" (src:7316-7317)
GIVEN `the person is an issuer within the meaning of Part 6 of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 (see section 102A(6))` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 519A(2) the person is an issuer` MEANS
    `the person is an issuer within the meaning of Part 6 of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 (see section 102A(6))`
    -- NOTHING here is -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "“issuer” has the same meaning as in Part 6 of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000"; JUST FALSE is that Act's no, supplied as an input

-- COVERS: s 519A(1), s 519A(1)"public interest company", s 519A(1)"public interest company"(a), s 519A(1)"public interest company"(b), s 519A(1)"public interest company"(c)
-- Plain gloss: a public interest company is a company that is (a) an issuer whose transferable securities are admitted to trading on a UK regulated market, or (b) a CRR credit institution, or (c) a person who would be an insurance undertaking in the EU sense were the United Kingdom a member State.
-- src:7311 | (1) In this Chapter—
-- src:7312 | “public interest company” means a company which is—
-- src:7313 | (a) an issuer whose transferable securities are admitted to trading on a UK regulated market;
-- src:7314 | (b) a credit institution within the meaning given by Article 4(1)(1) of Regulation (EU) No. 575/2013 of the European Parliament and of the Council, which is a CRR firm within the meaning of Article 4(1)(2A) of that Regulation; or
-- src:7315 | (c) a person who would be an insurance undertaking as defined in Article 2(1) of Council Directive 91/674/EEC of 19 December 1991 of the European Parliament and of the Council on the annual accounts and consolidated accounts of insurance undertakings as that Article had effect immediately before IP completion day, were the United Kingdom a member State;
@ref s 519A(1) "public interest company" (src:7311-7315)
GIVEN `s 519A(2) the company is an issuer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `its transferable securities are admitted to trading on a UK regulated market` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is a credit institution within the meaning given by Article 4(1)(1) of Regulation (EU) No. 575/2013 of the European Parliament and of the Council` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the credit institution is a CRR firm within the meaning of Article 4(1)(2A) of that Regulation` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the company is a person who would be an insurance undertaking as defined in Article 2(1) of Council Directive 91/674/EEC of 19 December 1991 ... as that Article had effect immediately before IP completion day, were the United Kingdom a member State` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 519A(1) the company is a public interest company` MEANS
    `coa12 either answer holds`
        (`coa12 either answer holds`
            (`coa12 both answers hold` `s 519A(2) the company is an issuer` (`coa12 the answer for the fact` `its transferable securities are admitted to trading on a UK regulated market`))
            (`coa12 both answers hold` `the company is a credit institution within the meaning given by Article 4(1)(1) of Regulation (EU) No. 575/2013 of the European Parliament and of the Council` `the credit institution is a CRR firm within the meaning of Article 4(1)(2A) of that Regulation`))
        `the company is a person who would be an insurance undertaking as defined in Article 2(1) of Council Directive 91/674/EEC of 19 December 1991 ... as that Article had effect immediately before IP completion day, were the United Kingdom a member State`
    -- JUST FALSE here is -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“public interest company” means a company which is— (a) ...; (b) ...; or (c) ..." (each borrowed answer is the other instrument's, supplied as an input)

-- COVERS-FORK F10: s 519A defines "non-public interest company"
-- Plain gloss: the heading promises a definition of "non-public interest company" but the body gives none. It is taken as a company that is not a public interest company (fork F10).
-- src:7310 | 519A Meaning of “public interest company”, “non-public interest company” and “exempt reasons”
@ref s 519A heading: "non-public interest company" (src:7310-7310)
GIVEN `s 519A(1) the company is a public interest company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 519A(1) the company is a non-public interest company` MEANS
    `coa12 the opposite answer` `s 519A(1) the company is a public interest company`
    -- NOTHING here is -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): the body of s 519A does not define "non-public interest company"; it is taken as the opposite of "public interest company" and the reading is flagged for a lawyer

-- s 519A(3): the reasons for ceasing to hold office that are "exempt reasons".
DECLARE `s 519A(3) reason for ceasing to hold office` HAS
    `s 519A(3)(a) A is no longer to carry out statutory audit work within the meaning of Part 42 (see section 1210(1))` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 519A(3)(b) the company is, or is to become, exempt from audit under section 477, 479A or 480, or from the requirements of this Part under section 482` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `s 519A(3)(b) the company intends to include in its balance sheet a statement of the type described in section 475(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 519A(3)(c) the company is a subsidiary undertaking of a parent undertaking that is incorporated in the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 519A(3)(c)(i) the parent undertaking prepares group accounts` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 519A(3)(c)(ii) A is being replaced as auditor of the company by the auditor who is conducting, or is to conduct, an audit of the group accounts` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 519A(4) that auditor is also conducting, or is also to conduct, the audit (if any) of the accounts of each of the UK subsidiary undertakings included in the consolidation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 519A(3)(d) the company is being wound up under Part 4 of the Insolvency Act 1986 or Part 5 of the Insolvency (Northern Ireland) Order 1989, whether voluntarily or by the court` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 519A(3)(d) a petition for the winding up of the company has been presented and not finally dealt with or withdrawn` IS A BOOLEAN

-- COVERS: s 519A(3), s 519A(3)(a), s 519A(3)(b), s 519A(3)(c), s 519A(3)(c)(i), s 519A(3)(c)(ii), s 519A(3)(d), s 519A(4), s 519A defines "exempt reasons"
-- Plain gloss: A's reasons for leaving are "exempt" if: he no longer does statutory audit work; the company is or will be exempt from audit and will say so in its balance sheet; the company is a UK subsidiary and he is being replaced by the group auditor, who also audits every UK subsidiary in the consolidation; or the company is being wound up or a winding-up petition is pending.
-- src:7320 | (3) In the application of this Chapter to an auditor (“A”) of a company ceasing to hold office, the following are “exempt reasons”—
-- src:7321 | (a) A is no longer to carry out statutory audit work within the meaning of Part 42 (see section 1210(1));
-- src:7322 | (b) the company is, or is to become, exempt from audit under section 477, 479A or 480, or from the requirements of this Part under section 482, and intends to include in its balance sheet a statement of the type described in section 475(2);
-- src:7323 | (c) the company is a subsidiary undertaking of a parent undertaking that is incorporated in the United Kingdom and—
-- src:7324 | (i) the parent undertaking prepares group accounts, and
-- src:7325 | (ii) A is being replaced as auditor of the company by the auditor who is conducting, or is to conduct, an audit of the group accounts;
-- src:7326 | (d) the company is being wound up under Part 4 of the Insolvency Act 1986 or Part 5 of the Insolvency (Northern Ireland) Order 1989 ( S.I. 1989/2405 (N.I. 19)), whether voluntarily or by the court, or a petition under Part 4 of that Act or Part 5 of that Order for the winding up of the company has been presented and not finally dealt with or withdrawn.
-- src:7327 | (4) But the reason described in subsection (3)(c) is only an exempt reason if the auditor who is conducting, or is to conduct, an audit of the group accounts is also conducting, or is also to conduct, the audit (if any) of the accounts of each of the subsidiary undertakings (of the parent undertaking) that is incorporated in the United Kingdom and included in the consolidation.
@ref s 519A(3)-(4) "exempt reasons" (src:7320-7327)
GIVEN reason IS A `s 519A(3) reason for ceasing to hold office`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 519A(3) the reason for ceasing to hold office is an exempt reason` MEANS
    `coa12 either answer holds`
        (`coa12 either answer holds`
            (`coa12 the answer for the fact` (reason's `s 519A(3)(a) A is no longer to carry out statutory audit work within the meaning of Part 42 (see section 1210(1))`))
            (`coa12 both answers hold` (reason's `s 519A(3)(b) the company is, or is to become, exempt from audit under section 477, 479A or 480, or from the requirements of this Part under section 482`) (`coa12 the answer for the fact` (reason's `s 519A(3)(b) the company intends to include in its balance sheet a statement of the type described in section 475(2)`))))
        (`coa12 either answer holds`
            (`coa12 the answer for the fact` (    (reason's `s 519A(3)(c) the company is a subsidiary undertaking of a parent undertaking that is incorporated in the United Kingdom`)
                                              AND (reason's `s 519A(3)(c)(i) the parent undertaking prepares group accounts`)
                                              AND (reason's `s 519A(3)(c)(ii) A is being replaced as auditor of the company by the auditor who is conducting, or is to conduct, an audit of the group accounts`)
                                              AND (reason's `s 519A(4) that auditor is also conducting, or is also to conduct, the audit (if any) of the accounts of each of the UK subsidiary undertakings included in the consolidation`)))
            (`coa12 the answer for the fact` (    (reason's `s 519A(3)(d) the company is being wound up under Part 4 of the Insolvency Act 1986 or Part 5 of the Insolvency (Northern Ireland) Order 1989, whether voluntarily or by the court`)
                                              OR  (reason's `s 519A(3)(d) a petition for the winding up of the company has been presented and not finally dealt with or withdrawn`))))
    -- JUST FALSE here is -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the following are “exempt reasons”— (a) ... (d) ..." (a list under "are", read as closed: fork F3) and "the reason described in subsection (3)(c) is only an exempt reason if the auditor who is conducting ... the audit of the group accounts is also conducting ... the audit ... of each of the subsidiary undertakings"

-- =========================================================================================================
-- s 519  Statement by auditor to be sent to company
-- =========================================================================================================

-- COVERS: s 519(1)
-- Plain gloss: an auditor of a public interest company who is ceasing to hold office, at any time and for any reason, must send the company a statement of his reasons.
-- src:7281 | (1) An auditor of a public interest company who is ceasing to hold office (at any time and for any reason) must send to the company a statement of the reasons for doing so.
@ref s 519(1) Public interest companies (src:7281-7281)
GIVEN `s 519A(1) the company is a public interest company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the auditor is ceasing to hold office (at any time and for any reason)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 519(1) the auditor of a public interest company must send the company a statement of the reasons` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 519A(1) the company is a public interest company`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF `the auditor is ceasing to hold office (at any time and for any reason)`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An auditor of a public interest company who is ceasing to hold office"
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty in (1) is for the auditor of a public interest company; subsection (2) governs a non-public interest company
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the company is a public interest company borrows terms of other instruments (s 519A)

-- COVERS: s 519(2A), s 519(2A)(a), s 519(2A)(b)
-- Plain gloss: the first condition is that A is ceasing to hold office at the end of a private company's period for appointing auditors, or at the end of a public company's accounts meeting.
-- src:7283 | (2A) The first condition is that A is ceasing to hold office—
-- src:7284 | (a) in the case of a private company, at the end of a period for appointing auditors;
-- src:7285 | (b) in the case of a public company, at the end of an accounts meeting.
@ref s 519(2A) The first condition (src:7283-7285)
GIVEN `s 4(1) the company is a private company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 485 Appointment of auditors of private company: general` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 4(2) the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 437 Public companies: laying of accounts and reports before general meeting` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 519(2A) the first condition is satisfied` MEANS
    `coa12 either answer holds`
        (IF `s 4(1) the company is a private company` THEN `s 485 Appointment of auditors of private company: general` ELSE JUST FALSE)
        (IF `s 4(2) the company is a public company` THEN `s 437 Public companies: laying of accounts and reports before general meeting` ELSE JUST FALSE)
    -- JUST FALSE here is -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The first condition is that A is ceasing to hold office— (a) in the case of a private company, at the end of a period for appointing auditors; (b) in the case of a public company, at the end of an accounts meeting."

-- A's reasons for ceasing to hold office are all exempt reasons: every reason in the list is one (an empty list states no reason: not covered).
GIVEN reasons IS A LIST OF `s 519A(3) reason for ceasing to hold office`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 519(2B)(a) every one of the reasons in the list is an exempt reason` MEANS
    CONSIDER reasons
    WHEN EMPTY THEN JUST TRUE -- the end of the list: nothing left to fail
    WHEN r FOLLOWED BY rest THEN `coa12 both answers hold` (`s 519A(3) the reason for ceasing to hold office is an exempt reason` r) (`s 519(2B)(a) every one of the reasons in the list is an exempt reason` rest)

-- COVERS: s 519(2B), s 519(2B)(a), s 519(2B)(b)
-- Plain gloss: the second condition is that all of A's reasons for leaving are exempt reasons and there are no matters connected with his leaving that A thinks members or creditors need to be told.
-- src:7286 | (2B) The second condition is that—
-- src:7287 | (a) A's reasons for ceasing to hold office are all exempt reasons (as to which see section 519A(3)), and
-- src:7288 | (b) there are no matters connected with A's ceasing to hold office that A considers need to be brought to the attention of members or creditors of the company.
@ref s 519(2B) The second condition (src:7286-7288)
GIVEN reasons IS A LIST OF `s 519A(3) reason for ceasing to hold office`
      `there are matters connected with A's ceasing to hold office that A considers need to be brought to the attention of members or creditors of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 519(2B) the second condition is satisfied` MEANS
    CONSIDER reasons
    WHEN EMPTY THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): no reason for ceasing to hold office is stated, so whether "A's reasons ... are all exempt reasons" is not decided
    OTHERWISE `coa12 both answers hold` (`s 519(2B)(a) every one of the reasons in the list is an exempt reason` reasons) (`coa12 the answer for the fact` (NOT `there are matters connected with A's ceasing to hold office that A considers need to be brought to the attention of members or creditors of the company`))
    -- JUST FALSE here is -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The second condition is that— (a) A's reasons for ceasing to hold office are all exempt reasons ..., and (b) there are no matters connected with A's ceasing to hold office that A considers need to be brought to the attention of members or creditors of the company."

-- COVERS: s 519(2)
-- Plain gloss: an auditor of a non-public interest company who is ceasing to hold office must send the company a statement of his reasons unless he satisfies the first or the second condition.
-- src:7282 | (2) An auditor (“A”) of a non-public interest company who is ceasing to hold office must send to the company a statement of the reasons for doing so unless A satisfies the first or second condition.
@ref s 519(2) Non-public interest companies (src:7282-7282)
GIVEN `s 519A(1) the company is a non-public interest company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the auditor is ceasing to hold office` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 519(2A) the first condition is satisfied` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 519(2B) the second condition is satisfied` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 519(2) the auditor of a non-public interest company must send the company a statement of the reasons` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 519A(1) the company is a non-public interest company` EQUALS JUST FALSE OR (NOT `the auditor is ceasing to hold office`) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An auditor (“A”) of a non-public interest company who is ceasing to hold office"; subsection (1) governs a public interest company
        IF `s 519A(1) the company is a non-public interest company` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): "non-public interest company" is not defined by s 519A (fork F10)
        IF `s 519(2A) the first condition is satisfied` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `s 519(2B) the second condition is satisfied` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must send to the company a statement of the reasons for doing so unless A satisfies the first or second condition" (an "unless" met: fork F6)
        IF `s 519(2A) the first condition is satisfied` EQUALS NOTHING OR `s 519(2B) the second condition is satisfied` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): a condition rests on an answer not known
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- COVERS: s 519(3), s 519(3)(a), s 519(3)(b), s 519(3)(c)
-- Plain gloss: the statement must give the auditor's name and address, the number allocated to him on the register of auditors (s 1239), and the company's name and registered number.
-- src:7289 | (3) A statement under this section must include—
-- src:7290 | (a) the auditor's name and address;
-- src:7291 | (b) the number allocated to the auditor on being entered in the register of auditors kept under section 1239;
-- src:7292 | (c) the company's name and registered number.
@ref s 519(3) What the statement must include (src:7289-7292)
GIVEN `the statement includes the auditor's name and address` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement includes the number allocated to the auditor on being entered in the register of auditors kept under section 1239` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement includes the company's name and registered number` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 519(3) the statement includes what the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF `the statement includes the auditor's name and address` AND `the statement includes the number allocated to the auditor on being entered in the register of auditors kept under section 1239` AND `the statement includes the company's name and registered number`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A statement under this section must include— (a) the auditor's name and address; (b) the number allocated to the auditor ...; (c) the company's name and registered number." (fork F2)

-- COVERS: s 519(3A)
-- Plain gloss: where there are matters connected with his leaving that the auditor thinks members or creditors need to be told, the statement must give details of them.
-- src:7293 | (3A) Where there are matters connected with an auditor's ceasing to hold office that the auditor considers need to be brought to the attention of members or creditors of the company, the statement under this section must include details of those matters.
@ref s 519(3A) Details of matters (src:7293-7293)
GIVEN `there are matters connected with an auditor's ceasing to hold office that the auditor considers need to be brought to the attention of members or creditors of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement includes details of those matters` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 519(3A) the statement includes the details the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF (NOT `there are matters connected with an auditor's ceasing to hold office that the auditor considers need to be brought to the attention of members or creditors of the company`)
    THEN JUST TRUE -- there are no such matters, so the subsection requires no details
    ELSE IF `the statement includes details of those matters`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the statement under this section must include details of those matters" (fork F2)

-- COVERS: s 519(3B), s 519(3B)(a), s 519(3B)(b), s 519(3B)#L7297
-- Plain gloss: where a non-public interest company's auditor must send a statement but considers that nothing about his leaving needs to be brought to members' or creditors' attention, the statement must say so.
-- src:7294 | (3B) Where—
-- src:7295 | (a) an auditor (“A”) of a non-public interest company is required by subsection (2) to send a statement, and
-- src:7296 | (b) A considers that none of the reasons for A's ceasing to hold office, and no matters (if any) connected with A's ceasing to hold office, need to be brought to the attention of members or creditors of the company,
-- src:7297 | A's statement under this section must include a statement to that effect.
@ref s 519(3B) The statement that nothing need be brought to attention (src:7294-7297)
GIVEN `an auditor of a non-public interest company is required by subsection (2) to send a statement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `A considers that none of the reasons for A's ceasing to hold office, and no matters (if any) connected with A's ceasing to hold office, need to be brought to the attention of members or creditors of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement includes a statement to that effect` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 519(3B) the statement includes the statement the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF (NOT (`an auditor of a non-public interest company is required by subsection (2) to send a statement` AND `A considers that none of the reasons for A's ceasing to hold office, and no matters (if any) connected with A's ceasing to hold office, need to be brought to the attention of members or creditors of the company`))
    THEN JUST TRUE -- the subsection's two conditions are not both met, so it requires no such statement
    ELSE IF `the statement includes a statement to that effect`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A's statement under this section must include a statement to that effect" (fork F2)

-- s 519(4): when the statement must be sent.
-- COVERS: s 519(4), s 519(4)(a)
-- Plain gloss: in the case of resignation, the statement goes along with the notice of resignation.
-- src:7298 | (4) A statement under this section must be sent—
-- src:7299 | (a) in the case of resignation, along with the notice of resignation;
@ref s 519(4)(a) Resignation: along with the notice (src:7298-7299)
GIVEN `the statement is sent along with the notice of resignation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 519(4)(a) the statement was sent in time on a resignation` MEANS
    IF `the statement is sent along with the notice of resignation`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A statement under this section must be sent— (a) in the case of resignation, along with the notice of resignation" (fork F2)

-- COVERS: s 519(4)(b)
-- Plain gloss: on a failure to seek re-appointment, the statement must be sent not less than 14 days before the end of the time allowed for next appointing an auditor: on or before the day 14 days earlier.
-- src:7298 | (4) A statement under this section must be sent—
-- src:7300 | (b) in the case of failure to seek re-appointment, not less than 14 days before the end of the time allowed for next appointing an auditor;
@ref s 519(4)(b) Failure to seek re-appointment: 14 days before the end of the time (src:7298-7300)
GIVEN `the date the statement is sent` IS A DATE
      `the end of the time allowed for next appointing an auditor` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 519(4)(b) the statement was sent in time on a failure to seek re-appointment` MEANS
    IF `the date the statement is sent` AT MOST (`the end of the time allowed for next appointing an auditor` MINUS 14)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "not less than 14 days before the end of the time allowed for next appointing an auditor" (a period fixed in the text's own words: the 2026-11-05 ruling (a); the day count is fork F9)

-- COVERS: s 519(4)(c)
-- Plain gloss: in any other case, not later than the end of the period of 14 days beginning with the date on which he ceases to hold office: the day he ceases and the 13 after it.
-- src:7298 | (4) A statement under this section must be sent—
-- src:7301 | (c) in any other case, not later than the end of the period of 14 days beginning with the date on which he ceases to hold office.
@ref s 519(4)(c) Any other case: 14 days beginning with the day he ceases (src:7298-7301)
GIVEN `the date on which he ceases to hold office` IS A DATE
      `the date the statement is sent` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 519(4)(c) the statement was sent in time in any other case` MEANS
    IF `the date the statement is sent` AT MOST (`the date on which he ceases to hold office` PLUS 13)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "not later than the end of the period of 14 days beginning with the date on which he ceases to hold office" (a period fixed in the text's own words: the 2026-11-05 ruling (a); the day count is fork F9)

-- The same duty as a deontic rule: day 0 is the day he ceases to hold office, and the 14th day of the period is day 13.
@ref s 519(4)(c) Any other case: 14 days beginning with the day he ceases (src:7298-7301)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Action of a party`
`s 519(4)(c) the auditor's duty to send the statement in any other case` MEANS
    PARTY Auditor
    MUST `Action of a party` OF Auditor, Company, "send the company a statement of the reasons for ceasing to hold office"
    WITHIN 13
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Auditor BECAUSE "s 519(4)(c): the statement was not sent within the period of 14 days beginning with the date on which he ceased to hold office"

-- COVERS: s 519(5)
-- Plain gloss: a person ceasing to hold office as auditor who fails to comply with s 519 commits an offence.
-- src:7302 | (5) A person ceasing to hold office as auditor who fails to comply with this section commits an offence.
@ref s 519(5) The offence (src:7302-7302)
GIVEN `the person is ceasing to hold office as auditor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person fails to comply with section 519` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 519(5) the person ceasing to hold office as auditor commits an offence` MEANS
    IF `the person is ceasing to hold office as auditor` AND `the person fails to comply with section 519`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person ceasing to hold office as auditor who fails to comply with this section commits an offence" (an offence defined by "who": marginal reading (a))

-- COVERS: s 519(6)
-- Plain gloss: it is a defence for the person charged to show that he took all reasonable steps and exercised all due diligence to avoid the offence.
-- src:7303 | (6) In proceedings for such an offence it is a defence for the person charged to show that he took all reasonable steps and exercised all due diligence to avoid the commission of the offence.
@ref s 519(6) The defence (src:7303-7303)
GIVEN `the person charged shows that he took all reasonable steps and exercised all due diligence to avoid the commission of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 519(6) the person charged has a defence under this subsection` MEANS
    IF `the person charged shows that he took all reasonable steps and exercised all due diligence to avoid the commission of the offence`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it is a defence for the person charged to show that he took all reasonable steps and exercised all due diligence" (the 2026-11-05 ruling (b): this section gives no defence on these facts)

-- COVERS: s 519(7), s 519(7)(a), s 519(7)(b)
-- Plain gloss: the penalty: on indictment a fine; on summary conviction a fine up to the statutory maximum.
-- src:7304 | (7) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable—
-- src:7305 | (a) on conviction on indictment, to a fine;
-- src:7306 | (b) on summary conviction, to a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum.
@ref s 519(7) The penalty (src:7304-7306)
GIVEN mode IS A `Mode of conviction`
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 519(7) the penalty for an offence under this section` MEANS
    CONSIDER mode
    WHEN `on conviction on indictment` THEN JUST (Penalty OF mode, NOTHING, JUST `a fine without a stated limit`, NOTHING, FALSE)
    OTHERWISE JUST (Penalty OF mode, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` OF 1), NOTHING, FALSE)

-- COVERS: s 519(8)
-- Plain gloss: where a body corporate commits the offence, every officer of the body who is in default also commits it.
-- src:7307 | (8) Where an offence under this section is committed by a body corporate, every officer of the body who is in default also commits the offence. For this purpose—
@ref s 519(8) Officers of a body corporate (src:7307-7307)
GIVEN `the offence under this section is committed by a body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 519(8) the officer of the body corporate also commits the offence` MEANS
    IF `the offence under this section is committed by a body corporate`
    THEN `s 1121 the officer is in default` -- JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE (not in default: section 1121), or NOTHING where section 1121 is not known
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an offence under this section is committed by a body corporate, every officer of the body who is in default also commits the offence" (the 2026-11-05 ruling on "where")

