-- The duty as a deontic rule: either alternative within 14 days of receipt (day 0), or breach.
@ref s 520(2) The company must send a copy or apply to the court (src:7334-7336)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Action of a party`
`s 520(2) the company's duty to send a copy of the statement or apply to the court` MEANS
    (PARTY Company
     MUST `Action of a party` OF Company, Member, "send a copy of the statement to every person who under section 423 is entitled to be sent copies of the accounts"
     WITHIN 14
     HENCE FULFILLED
     LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "s 520(2): no copy was sent")
    ROR
    (PARTY Company
     MUST `Action of a party` OF Company, Court, "apply to the court"
     WITHIN 14
     HENCE FULFILLED
     LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "s 520(2): no application was made")

