    WHEN `on conviction on indictment` THEN JUST (Penalty OF mode, NOTHING, JUST `a fine without a stated limit`, NOTHING, FALSE)
    OTHERWISE JUST (Penalty OF mode, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` OF 1), NOTHING, FALSE)

-- COVERS: s 521(6)
-- Plain gloss: where a body corporate commits the offence, every officer of the body who is in default also commits it.
-- src:7359 | (6) Where an offence under this section is committed by a body corporate, every officer of the body who is in default also commits the offence. For this purpose—
@ref s 521(6) Officers of a body corporate (src:7359-7359)
GIVEN `the offence under this section is committed by a body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 521(6) the officer of the body corporate also commits the offence` MEANS
    IF `the offence under this section is committed by a body corporate`
    THEN `s 1121 the officer is in default` -- JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE (not in default: section 1121), or NOTHING where section 1121 is not known
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an offence under this section is committed by a body corporate, every officer of the body who is in default also commits the offence" (the 2026-11-05 ruling on "where")

-- COVERS: s 521(6)(a)
-- Plain gloss: for this purpose a person who purports to act as director, manager or secretary of the body is treated as an officer of the body.
-- src:7360 | (a) any person who purports to act as director, manager or secretary of the body is treated as an officer of the body, and
@ref s 521(6)(a) Purporting to act (src:7360-7360)
GIVEN `the person purports to act as director, manager or secretary of the body` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 521(6)(a) the person is treated as an officer of the body` MEANS
    IF `the person purports to act as director, manager or secretary of the body`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the paragraph treats those persons as officers and does not say no one else is one

-- COVERS: s 521(6)(b)
-- Plain gloss: if the body is a company, any shadow director is treated as an officer of the company.
-- src:7361 | (b) if the body is a company, any shadow director is treated as an officer of the company.
@ref s 521(6)(b) Shadow directors (src:7361-7361)
GIVEN `the body is a company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 251 the person is a shadow director` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 521(6)(b) the shadow director is treated as an officer of the company` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the body is a company`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the body is a company, any shadow director is treated as an officer of the company" (marginal reading (a))
    ELSE CONSIDER `s 251 the person is a shadow director`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the paragraph treats a shadow director as an officer and does not say no one else is one
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person is a shadow director is section 251 (coa5), not known

