GIVEN `s 4(1) the company is a private company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 485 Appointment of auditors of private company: general` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 4(2) the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 437 Public companies: laying of accounts and reports before general meeting` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 523(1) the section applies where the auditor is ceasing to hold office` MEANS
    `coa12 either answer holds`
        (IF `s 4(1) the company is a private company` THEN `coa12 the opposite answer` `s 485 Appointment of auditors of private company: general` ELSE JUST FALSE)
        (IF `s 4(2) the company is a public company` THEN `coa12 the opposite answer` `s 437 Public companies: laying of accounts and reports before general meeting` ELSE JUST FALSE)
    -- JUST FALSE here is -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies if an auditor is ceasing to hold office— (a) in the case of a private company, at any time other than at the end of a period for appointing auditors; (b) in the case of a public company, at any time other than at the end of an accounts meeting."

