    BRANCH
        IF `s 523(1) the section applies where the auditor is ceasing to hold office` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where this section applies, the company must give notice" (the 2026-11-05 ruling on "where"; fork F1)
        IF `s 523(1A) the section does not apply` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "But this section does not apply if the company reasonably believes ..."
        IF `s 523(1) the section applies where the auditor is ceasing to hold office` EQUALS NOTHING OR `s 523(1A) the section does not apply` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the section applies rests on an answer not known
