-- COVERS: s 523(2A), s 523(2A)#L7379, s 523(2B), s 523(2B)(a), s 523(2B)(b), s 523(2B)(c), s 523(2C)
-- Plain gloss: the notice is a statement by the company of what it believes the reasons are, with the information listed in s 519(3); but where the company has received the auditor's s 519 statement in time and agrees with it, the notice may instead be a copy of that statement endorsed to say the company agrees.
-- src:7378 | (2A) The notice is to take the form of a statement by the company of what the company believes to be the reasons for the auditor's ceasing to hold office and must include the information listed in section 519(3).
-- src:7379 | This is subject to subsection (2C).
-- src:7380 | (2B) Subsection (2C) applies where—
-- src:7381 | (a) the company receives a statement from the auditor under section 519,
-- src:7382 | (b) the statement is sent at the time required by section 519(4), and
-- src:7383 | (c) the company agrees with the contents of the statement.
-- src:7384 | (2C) Where this subsection applies, the notice may instead take the form of a copy of the statement endorsed by the company to the effect that it agrees with the contents of the statement.
@ref s 523(2A)-(2C) The form of the notice (src:7378-7384)
GIVEN `the notice is a statement by the company of what the company believes to be the reasons for the auditor's ceasing to hold office` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice includes the information listed in section 519(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company receives a statement from the auditor under section 519` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement is sent at the time required by section 519(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company agrees with the contents of the statement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice is a copy of the statement endorsed by the company to the effect that it agrees with the contents of the statement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
