    IF `the notice is a statement by the company of what the company believes to be the reasons for the auditor's ceasing to hold office` AND `the notice includes the information listed in section 519(3)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF `the company receives a statement from the auditor under section 519` AND `the statement is sent at the time required by section 519(4)` AND `the company agrees with the contents of the statement` AND `the notice is a copy of the statement endorsed by the company to the effect that it agrees with the contents of the statement`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The notice is to take the form of a statement by the company of what the company believes to be the reasons ... and must include the information listed in section 519(3). This is subject to subsection (2C)" and "the notice may instead take the form of a copy of the statement endorsed by the company" (fork F2: a bare "must")

