    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the court has made an order under section 520(4) directing that copies of the statement need not be sent out by the company, sections 460 and 461 ... apply" (marginal reading (a))

-- =========================================================================================================
-- s 525  Meaning of "appropriate audit authority"
-- The text shows two paragraphs lettered (a) (lines 7404 and 7407); both are encoded, and the answer is a list (fork F8).
-- =========================================================================================================

DECLARE `s 525(1) audit authority` IS ONE OF
    `s 525(1)(a)(i) the Secretary of State`
    `s 525(1)(a)(ii) the body to which the Secretary of State has delegated functions under section 1252`
    `s 525(1)(a) the Financial Reporting Council Limited`
    `s 525(1)(b) the relevant supervisory body`
    `s 525(1)(c) the Independent Supervisor`

-- COVERS-FORK F8: s 525(1), s 525(1)(a), s 525(1)(a)(i), s 525(1)(a)(ii), s 525(1)(a)#L7407, s 525(1)(b), s 525(1)(c), s 525 defines "appropriate audit authority"
-- Plain gloss: for an auditor of a public interest company (not an Auditor General) the authority is the Secretary of State or, if he has delegated the function to a body whose functions include receiving the statement or notice, that body; for a major audit not conducted by an Auditor General, the Financial Reporting Council Limited; for an auditor of a non-public interest company (not an Auditor General), the relevant supervisory body; for an Auditor General, the Independent Supervisor.
-- src:7403 | (1) In sections 522, 523 and 524 “appropriate audit authority” means—
-- src:7404 | (a) in relation to an auditor of a public interest company (other than an Auditor General)—
-- src:7405 | (i) the Secretary of State, or
-- src:7406 | (ii) if the Secretary of State has delegated functions under section 1252 to a body whose functions include receiving the statement or notice in question, that body;
-- src:7407 | (a) in the case of a major audit (other than one conducted by an Auditor General), the Financial Reporting Council Limited;
-- src:7408 | (b) in relation to an auditor of a non-public interest company (other than an Auditor General), the relevant supervisory body.
-- src:7409 | (c) in relation to an Auditor General, the Independent Supervisor.
@ref s 525(1) "appropriate audit authority" (src:7403-7409)
GIVEN `s 519A(1) the company is a public interest company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the auditor is an Auditor General` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary of State has delegated functions under section 1252 to a body whose functions include receiving the statement or notice in question` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the audit is a major audit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE (LIST OF `s 525(1) audit authority`)
`s 525(1) the appropriate audit authority` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 519A(1) the company is a public interest company`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the company is a public interest company borrows terms of other instruments (s 519A), and the answer depends on it
    WHEN JUST pic THEN
        JUST
            (append
                (IF pic AND (NOT `the auditor is an Auditor General`)
                 THEN (IF `the Secretary of State has delegated functions under section 1252 to a body whose functions include receiving the statement or notice in question`
                       THEN LIST `s 525(1)(a)(ii) the body to which the Secretary of State has delegated functions under section 1252`
                       ELSE LIST `s 525(1)(a)(i) the Secretary of State`)
                 ELSE EMPTY)
                (append
                    (IF `the audit is a major audit` AND (NOT `the auditor is an Auditor General`) THEN LIST `s 525(1)(a) the Financial Reporting Council Limited` ELSE EMPTY)
                    (append
                        (IF (NOT pic) AND (NOT `the auditor is an Auditor General`) THEN LIST `s 525(1)(b) the relevant supervisory body` ELSE EMPTY)
                        (IF `the auditor is an Auditor General` THEN LIST `s 525(1)(c) the Independent Supervisor` ELSE EMPTY))))
    -- an empty list is "no limb names an authority for these facts": limited by its own wording

-- COVERS: s 525(1)"Supervisory body"
-- Plain gloss: "supervisory body" and "Independent Supervisor" mean what Part 42 says (ss 1217 and 1228): borrowed answers, taken as inputs.
-- src:7410 | “Supervisory body” and “Independent Supervisor” have the same meaning as in Part 42 (statutory auditors) (see sections 1217 and 1228).
@ref s 525(1) "Supervisory body" and "Independent Supervisor" (src:7410-7410)
GIVEN `s 1217 Supervisory bodies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 525(1) the body is a supervisory body` MEANS
    `s 1217 Supervisory bodies`
    -- NOTHING here is -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "“Supervisory body” ... [has] the same meaning as in Part 42"; JUST FALSE is Part 42's no, supplied as an input

@ref s 525(1) "Independent Supervisor" (src:7410-7410)
GIVEN `s 1228 Appointment of the Independent Supervisor` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 525(1) the person is the Independent Supervisor` MEANS
    `s 1228 Appointment of the Independent Supervisor`
    -- NOTHING here is -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "“Independent Supervisor” ... [has] the same meaning as in Part 42"; JUST FALSE is Part 42's no, supplied as an input

