-- s 526  Effect of casual vacancies
-- =========================================================================================================

-- COVERS: s 526#L7415
-- Plain gloss: if an auditor ceases to hold office for any reason, any surviving or continuing auditor or auditors may continue to act.
-- src:7415 | If an auditor ceases to hold office for any reason, any surviving or continuing auditor or auditors may continue to act.
@ref s 526 Effect of casual vacancies (src:7415-7415)
GIVEN `an auditor ceases to hold office for any reason` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a surviving or continuing auditor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 526 the surviving or continuing auditor may continue to act` MEANS
    IF (NOT `an auditor ceases to hold office for any reason`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If an auditor ceases to hold office for any reason, any surviving or continuing auditor or auditors may continue to act." (fork F16: a grant named "may" whose plain "if" gate fails; the other reading is JUST FALSE)
    ELSE IF `the person is a surviving or continuing auditor`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any surviving or continuing auditor or auditors may continue to act"
